WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
A new single-cell sequencing method maps both intended and unintended CRISPR edits along with their effects on gene activity. This is Planetterrian Daily, Episode 246. Young people's health in the United Kingdom, vitamin C after meals, and waste water from Ohio City's follow. Salk Institute scientists develop superb seek in work covered by Fies.org and ran it on 34,000 cells from three cell lines. The method combines Cas9 editing, a short edit reporting DNA sequence.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:36.380
and single cell RNA sequencing, so each cell carries both a record of where DNA was cut and

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:38.400
a readout of which genes were then active.

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:45.440
In one group of 10,000 human leukemia cells, superb seek identified 43 edit sites and detected

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:48.300
5,761 edited cells.

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:53.980
36 of those 43 sites were off-target, and the same assay distinguished edits likely

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:58.660
to be benign from those that disrupt genes protecting against cancer or other disorders.

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:03.400
The study was published in Nature Methods on November 16, 2026.

00:01:04.377 --> 00:01:09.157
People ages 16 to 24 in the United Kingdom were tracked by University College London

00:01:09.157 --> 00:01:14.917
researchers in the UK household longitudinal study between 2009 and 2023.

00:01:15.457 --> 00:01:20.357
The data set covered more than 15,000 people, and the share reporting a health problem

00:01:20.357 --> 00:01:28.517
or disability rose from about 4% in 2014 through 2018 to about 9% in 2019 through 2023.

00:01:28.517 --> 00:01:35.677
Reports of psychological distress increased from about 18% to about 21% over those same periods,

00:01:36.177 --> 00:01:40.737
and those prevalence shifts accounted for a greater share of young people not in work, education,

00:01:41.137 --> 00:01:45.877
or training. The likelihood that a person with a health problem would be out of work, education,

00:01:46.197 --> 00:01:51.497
or training remained unchanged between the two periods. Levels of clinical depression rose

00:01:51.497 --> 00:01:58.037
and fell in step with those not in work rates across 2022 and 2023. The study concluded that

00:01:58.037 --> 00:02:02.497
interventions focused only on the labor market are unlikely to reverse the trend without

00:02:02.497 --> 00:02:05.977
concurrent investment in mental health prevention and treatment access.

00:02:06.337 --> 00:02:11.897
A mathematical model covered by science daily indicates that vitamin C taken after meals

00:02:12.197 --> 00:02:17.477
can lower the formation of potentially cancer-causing chemicals from nitrates and nitrites in food.

00:02:18.017 --> 00:02:22.877
The model focuses on reactions that occur in the stomach after nitrate and nitrite-containing

00:02:22.877 --> 00:02:23.237
meals.

00:02:23.877 --> 00:02:28.357
The researchers who built the model suggest that the timing of vitamin C intake could

00:02:28.357 --> 00:02:34.268
offer a strategy for lowering cancer risk. Analysis of wastewater bacteria from eight Ohio

00:02:34.268 --> 00:02:40.568
cities serving 1.3 million people reported via science subreddit found gut microbiome

00:02:40.568 --> 00:02:45.968
patterns associated with local rates of obesity, high blood pressure, asthma, and depression.

00:02:46.828 --> 00:02:51.428
Zebrafish spines showed blocked mineral accumulation when researchers used an existing

00:02:51.428 --> 00:02:57.488
osteoporosis drug. In work covered by science daily, after they identified a genetic link to

00:02:57.488 --> 00:03:02.848
spinal degeneration. The finding points to a possible route for slowing or preventing a major

00:03:02.848 --> 00:03:09.137
contributor to chronic back pain. An international team including McGill University researchers recovered

00:03:09.137 --> 00:03:15.337
remarkably large rodent fossils from a mine pit in southern Thailand. In findings, Fizz.org notes

00:03:15.337 --> 00:03:21.097
were published in scientific reports. The fossils show that rodent gigantism began earlier than

00:03:21.097 --> 00:03:26.637
previously recognized, and that it occurred across a wider geographic range than earlier work had

00:03:26.637 --> 00:03:33.199
mapped. A well-preserved skeleton from Mesolithic Denmark was dated with radio-carbon methods and

00:03:33.199 --> 00:03:38.559
read with isotope analysis. The individual lived through the introduction of agriculture and changed

00:03:38.559 --> 00:03:44.059
diet accordingly, and the remains provided direct record of one person's adaptation during the

00:03:44.059 --> 00:03:50.840
Neolithic transition. In areas with high segregation, the specific school of child attends is closely

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:56.400
tied to how many years of education parents expect that child to complete. Higher school segregation

00:03:56.400 --> 00:04:01.100
strengthens that link between the school attended and those expected years of education.

00:04:02.199 --> 00:04:06.819
Researchers use laboratory models to examine how falling rocks and ash interact with

00:04:06.819 --> 00:04:12.279
seawater to produce waves. The work addresses gaps in understanding the complex dynamics that

00:04:12.279 --> 00:04:17.959
determine whether a volcanic flow will trigger a tsunami and how large any resulting wave may be.

00:04:18.833 --> 00:04:24.393
Cross-border fertility care in Czechia was reduced during the pandemic period. A new study reported

00:04:24.393 --> 00:04:29.573
be a science subreddit documents. Most people assume that when human carbon dioxide emissions

00:04:29.573 --> 00:04:35.193
fall to zero, global temperature will soon flatten or drop. But a Met Office Hadley Center

00:04:35.193 --> 00:04:40.893
study covered by Fizz.org found that the temperature change after emissions stop is not uniformly

00:04:40.893 --> 00:04:46.433
close to zero. That later change has a name, the Zero Emissions Commitment, and it varies

00:04:46.433 --> 00:04:51.113
with the amount of warming that has already taken place. The team examined the relationship

00:04:51.113 --> 00:04:56.253
across multiple climate models rather than in a single run, comparing model worlds that

00:04:56.253 --> 00:05:01.213
reach different warming levels before emissions were cut. When substantial warming has already

00:05:01.213 --> 00:05:06.193
occurred, the committed temperature change can remain positive even after emissions reached

00:05:06.193 --> 00:05:11.413
net zero. Before we go, new temperature and emissions records are released each year,

00:05:11.793 --> 00:05:16.153
and those observations will show how they line up with these zero emissions model patterns.

